## Anti-Patterns

| Anti-Pattern | Why It's Bad | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| **Unwired tool loops** | LLM calls tools but graph routes past them | Add `ToolNode` + conditional edge + loop-back |
| **Unconditional step advancement in wait nodes** | No multi-turn conversations within step | Check state before advancing `currentStep` |
| **State mutation in nodes** | Breaks reducer merge logic | Return new partial state objects |
| **Side effects in nodes (DB writes)** | Breaks replay semantics | Use checkpointer for persistence |
| **Blocking operations in nodes** | Blocks event loop | Use `interrupt()` + resume pattern |
| **Side effects in routing functions** | Non-deterministic routing | Pure inspection only |
| **God nodes** | Multiple responsibilities | Split into focused single-purpose nodes |
| **Missing tool-loop guard** | Infinite loops burn tokens | `__tool_loop_iteration` counter + max 10 |
| **Manual DB writes + checkpointer** | Double-write, inconsistent state | Choose one — use checkpointer |

